<DocsLayout title="API reference" description="HTTP endpoints for scripting, automation, and third-party integrations with Tome.">
  <SectionHero section="integrations" />
  <h1>API reference</h1>
  <p>
    Every endpoint lives under <code>/api</code> and accepts either a JWT (from login) or a <code>tome_*</code> bearer token. See <a href={withBase("/docs/api-tokens")}>API tokens</a> for how to create one. All request/response bodies are JSON unless noted.
  </p>
  <DocsMeta />

  <Callout variant="info" title="Base URL">
    All paths below are relative to your Tome instance, e.g. <code>https://tome.example.com/api/books</code>.
  </Callout>

  <h2>Auth</h2>
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>Method</th><th>Path</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td><code>POST</code></td><td><code>/api/auth/login</code></td><td>Authenticate, returns a JWT that stays valid until signed out. Each call is a new sign-in listed under Settings &gt; Connected devices, so scripts should use an API token instead</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>POST</code></td><td><code>/api/auth/logout</code></td><td>End the calling sign-in</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>GET</code></td><td><code>/api/auth/me</code></td><td>Current user profile, including <code>week_start</code> (<code>monday</code> / <code>sunday</code>)</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>PUT</code></td><td><code>/api/auth/me</code></td><td>Update username / email / <code>week_start</code></td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>PUT</code></td><td><code>/api/auth/me/password</code></td><td>Change password</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>GET</code></td><td><code>/api/auth/me/stats</code></td><td>Reading stats for current user</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>GET</code></td><td><code>/api/auth/me/backup</code></td><td>Export user data as JSON</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

